# Kernel config addition needed for Phosh to start at all - this device's
# stock kernel .config had CONFIG_VT explicitly unset. Found by direct
# testing: phosh.service's own ConditionPathExists=/dev/tty0 failed, and
# even with that condition bypassed (a local systemd drop-in), the real
# phosh-session process itself failed (status=208/STDIN - needs a real
# controlling tty) and its ExecStartPost `chvt 7` failed outright (no VT
# subsystem at all to switch on). See docs/display.md for the full evidence
# trail, including confirmation via the official Droidian/Phosh docs that
# ConditionPathExists=/dev/tty0 is a genuine, documented requirement, not
# something specific to this device.
#
# IMPORTANT - this device's build.sh has a documented history of a real
# crash from a PREVIOUS attempt at "VT/FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE" together (see
# the comment this replaces in build.sh, and
# docs/history/session-journal-2026-08.md's account of an early
# generic-framebuffer-console experiment crashing against Samsung's own
# DRM/panel driver). Before re-attempting, this session read the actual
# decon driver source (drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_notify.c) to
# confirm WHY that earlier attempt crashed and why THIS narrower change is
# safe:
#   - decon only registers with the fbdev notifier chain (fb_register_client
#     / decon_fb_notifier_event, blank_early, blank_after) - this chain is
#     ONLY ever driven by CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE's own blank/mode-change
#     activity, never by bare VT/dummy-console switching.
#   - `grep -rl register_vt_notifier` across the ENTIRE drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/
#     tree found NOTHING - decon has no direct VT-notifier hook of any kind.
#   - Therefore: CONFIG_VT alone (letting CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE and
#     CONFIG_DUMMY_CONSOLE auto-select via their own Kconfig `default y`
#     logic) never touches decon's registered callback at all.
#     CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE (fbcon) - the thing that actually crashed
#     before - is deliberately NOT re-added here.
CONFIG_VT=y
#
# CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE and CONFIG_DUMMY_CONSOLE are NOT set explicitly here -
# both `default y` once CONFIG_VT=y is set (verified in
# drivers/tty/Kconfig and drivers/video/console/Kconfig respectively), and
# letting them auto-select is exactly what keeps CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE
# out of the picture (DUMMY_CONSOLE is the safe do-nothing console that
# claims the VT instead, when no VGA/fbcon driver is present).
#
# CONFIRMED after the rebuild, not assumed - this project's own repeated
# lesson (Kconfig silently drops a symbol whose dependencies aren't met,
# with no build error):
#   CONFIG_VT=y
#   CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE=y
#   CONFIG_DUMMY_CONSOLE=y
#   (CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE genuinely absent - grep found nothing)
#
# CONFIRMED live on real hardware after flashing:
#   - /dev/tty0 exists
#   - /sys/class/vtconsole/vtcon0/name = "(S) dummy device" (dummy bound,
#     not fbcon - the specific thing that crashed before)
#   - Android LXC container still State: RUNNING - no regression
#   - phosh.service starts and stays active (running); phoc (the wlroots
#     compositor) composited and presented one real, correctly-sized frame
#     to the physical panel - confirmed via /sys/kernel/debug/decon/event0
#     (WIN_CONFIG / FENCE_ACQUIRE / UPDATE_HANDLER Partial Size
#     (0,0,1080,2340)) AND visually on the device screen.
#
# Apply the same way as kernel/07-kernel-config-lxc-networking.config - as
# an echo line in build.sh's config-injection block (see that file's own
# "Disable Samsung integrity/anti-exploit subsystems" section, where this
# was actually added).
